## 3. Tier 1: Resilient Native Adaptive Icon (App Drawer & System Launcher)

To ensure animations remain smooth when opening and closing the app from the drawer, the native icon must avoid clipping, stretching, or showing empty borders.

### Physics and Geometry Rules

1. **Total Canvas**: $108 \times 108\,\text{dp}$.
2. **Safe Viewport**: $72\,\text{dp}$ centered circle. All critical content (Squircle container, hands, arrow, bubble) is anchored strictly within a $66\,\text{dp}$ bounding box inside the safe zone.
3. **Bleed Zone ($66\,\text{dp} \rightarrow 108\,\text{dp}$)**: The background layer extends its deep navy base (`#071126`) and outer aura outward to the full $108\,\text{dp}$ margin. When modern launchers (Pixel Launcher, One UI, HyperOS) apply spring physics, parallax motion, or squircle-to-fullscreen morphing, no blank canvas or transparent seams are exposed.

