## 4. Tier 2: The 1x1 Zero-Drain Real-Time Live Micro-Tile

The live home screen experience is delivered via a specialized 1x1 micro-tile that runs inside the system launcher's process rather than relying on background execution.

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        LAUNCHER PROCESS (SystemUI)                     │
│                                                                        │
│   ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│   │ RemoteViews (Model 3 FrameLayout - 1x1 Tile)                   │   │
│   │                                                                │   │
│   │   • android.widget.AnalogClock                                 │   │
│   │     - Custom Dial Drawable (@drawable/widget_dial)             │   │
│   │     - Vector Hour Hand     (@drawable/widget_hand_hour)        │   │
│   │     - Vector Minute Hand   (@drawable/widget_hand_minute)      │   │
│   │     - Vector Second Hand   (@drawable/widget_hand_second)      │   │
│   │                                                                │   │
│   │   • android.widget.TextClock                                   │   │
│   │     - Formats: "HH:mm" / "h:mm"                                │   │
│   │     - Positioned precisely over Green Pebble Bubble            │   │
│   │     - Native hardware-rendered font (No bitmap generation)     │   │
│   │                                                                │   │
│   │   • Root PendingIntent -> Launch MainActivity with             │   │
│   │     ActivityOptionsCompat.makeScaleUpAnimation                 │   │
│   └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                                                                        │
│   Runs 100% on Launcher Thread  •  Zero Battery Drain  •  Never Freezes│
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

```

### Why This Solution is Bulletproof

* **Zero App Process Overhead**: `AnalogClock` and `TextClock` are evaluated directly by the host launcher. The app can be force-stopped, cached, or battery-restricted by HyperOS; the clock hands and the digital time bubble will continue ticking smoothly and accurately without interruption.
* **Pixel-Exact Icon Simulation**: The widget is locked to $1 \times 1$ grid dimensions with launcher margins removed (`android:widgetFeatures="reconfigurable|hide_preview"`). It uses the exact Model 3 squircle silhouette, appearing visually identical to an application icon.
* **Seamless Touch Physics**: The root container executes a `PendingIntent` wired to `ActivityOptionsCompat.makeScaleUpAnimation()`, ensuring the open/close transition expands smoothly from the tile's bounding box just like a standard app launch.

